        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_69d0f8ad63dc464481202d9e35008c04",
      "statement": "`UserApiClient` is the dedicated outbound integration boundary and issues fixed requests against the configured base URL for collection reads, item reads, create, update, delete, deactivate, and activate operations.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/com/example/consumer/client/UserApiClient.java#L14-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c96f8ada51385ef69cdd78553385177bd5ab26972fb70de5b91ce147c7e37f6a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3d9340f3513c4a48bc7a12ad530e3c7b",
      "statement": "The consumer invokes `GET /api/users` and `GET /api/users/active` as collection reads, deserializing each response body into `List<User>` via `RestTemplate.exchange(...)` and `ParameterizedTypeReference<List<User>>() {}`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/com/example/consumer/client/UserApiClient.java#L25-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:010156933032e2bde09998a2bd18eba758a9efec0de5a801e111db1a5820741a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7212573565334d4eba7518c0c88b7b25",
      "statement": "The consumer reads individual users with `GET /api/users/{id}` and `GET /api/users/username/{username}`, both via `RestTemplate.getForObject(...)` into `User`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/com/example/consumer/client/UserApiClient.java#L44-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c3bc17a50e06b5b495527a268da4278d0c1b85aefad9b360907a64f5d2ab6dcb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_71635ef78ebb42539a5ac6e89ca77472",
      "statement": "The consumer creates users with `POST /api/users` and expects a `User` response, while update and delete use `PUT /api/users/{id}` and `DELETE /api/users/{id}` without inspecting a response body.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/com/example/consumer/client/UserApiClient.java#L59-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:589917a56587868d803611ed8981d13e6dd35c2fc10eabcf8d03e66c2eeb3f86:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5af3657a068844388c6ae24c806203c5",
      "statement": "The consumer activates and deactivates users with `PATCH /api/users/{id}/activate` and `PATCH /api/users/{id}/deactivate`, sending `null` bodies and ignoring any returned content.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/com/example/consumer/client/UserApiClient.java#L78-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8c50e0205eb1c4fe89a230ea4f489d28ff082b95e90f6d427b038cf5c65a0f76:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_815c07ccc49547b1ac5ce7d00413edf4",
      "statement": "The client does not implement explicit null or empty guards for remote responses; collection reads return `response.getBody()` directly and the single-item reads delegate missing-response behavior to Spring's `RestTemplate` methods.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/com/example/consumer/client/UserApiClient.java#L25-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0c1b23b6431ba604a742a4ee5d9f3df36d64379537839b98c800441d852ac9e4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_58200e96e6ce42cca040e484010ab1a5",
      "statement": "The consumer assumes the producer returns plain `User` objects and JSON arrays of `User` for these endpoints, rather than a paged wrapper or another envelope shape.",
